---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

const siteURL = "https://dearwander.com";

const personSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Person",
  "name": "Gabriela Martínez",
  "jobTitle": "Founder & Engineer, Dear Wander",
  "description":
    "Computer engineer and founder of Dear Wander, a mindful screen time app for iOS. Writes about the science of attention, anxiety, and calm.",
  "alumniOf": {
    "@type": "CollegeOrUniversity",
    "name": "Universidad Simón Bolívar",
    "address": "Caracas, Venezuela",
  },
  "knowsAbout": [
    "digital wellbeing",
    "screen time",
    "attention science",
    "anxiety",
    "mindful technology",
  ],
  "worksFor": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "Dear Wander", "url": siteURL },
  "url": `${siteURL}/about`,
};

const aboutSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "AboutPage",
  "name": "About Dear Wander",
  "url": `${siteURL}/about`,
  "mainEntity": personSchema,
};
---

<Layout
  title="About — Dear Wander"
  description="Dear Wander is built by Gabriela Martínez, a computer engineer from Caracas, out of her own experience with anxiety and a restless relationship with the phone. A gentler approach to screen time."
>
  <Header lightBg={true} />

  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(personSchema)} />
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(aboutSchema)} />

  <main class="pt-32 pb-20 px-6 bg-golden-hour min-h-screen">
    <article class="max-w-2xl mx-auto prose prose-earth">
      <h1 class="font-wander text-4xl text-earth mb-6">About Dear Wander</h1>

      <p class="text-lg text-taupe font-light mb-10">
        Dear Wander is a small, deliberate thing, built by someone who needed it first.
      </p>

      <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-10 not-prose">
        <div
          class="w-16 h-16 rounded-full bg-breath text-warm-white flex items-center justify-center font-serif font-semibold text-lg flex-shrink-0"
        >
          GM
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="font-serif font-semibold text-earth text-lg leading-tight">Gabriela Martínez</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-taupe">Founder &amp; engineer · Computer engineer, Universidad Simón Bolívar (Caracas, Venezuela)</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Why this exists</h2>
      <p>
        I'm Gabriela. I trained as a computer engineer at the Universidad Simón Bolívar in Caracas,
        and for a long time I built things that were clever without asking whether they were kind.
      </p>
      <p>
        Dear Wander started somewhere more personal than a product roadmap. It came out of my own
        years of managing anxiety, and of noticing how often the phone was both the reach for relief
        and the thing that left me more frayed than before. The scroll was never really about the
        content. It was about avoiding a feeling. And every app I tried to help me stop treated me
        like a problem to be disciplined: red numbers, broken streaks, locked screens that made me
        feel worse and scroll more.
      </p>
      <p>
        I wanted to build the opposite. Something gentle. Something that assumes you're a capable
        person having a hard moment, not a failure who needs to be punished into behaving. I care
        especially about making that softness available to women, who so often carry the quiet weight
        of anxiety and are handed tools built around shame.
      </p>

      <h2>The idea, in one line</h2>
      <p>
        A warm sixty-second breathing pause before the apps that pull at you. No lock, no timer, no
        report card. Just a small gap between the reach and the tap, where the choice becomes yours
        again. Most of the time, after a breath, you choose something else.
      </p>

      <h2>How I write these articles</h2>
      <p>
        I'm an engineer and a founder, not a doctor. What I can do is read the research carefully and
        translate it into plain language you can actually use, with sources you can check yourself. When
        I cite a study, a statistic, or a mechanism, I link to where it comes from. I use writing tools
        to help me draft and structure, but every article is shaped, fact-checked, and edited by me, and
        reflects what I've genuinely learned building this and living it.
      </p>
      <p>
        If something here is ever wrong, I want to fix it. You can reach me at
        <a href="mailto:hello@dearwander.com">hello@dearwander.com</a> or on Instagram at
        <a href="https://instagram.com/dearwander.app" target="_blank" rel="noopener">@dearwander.app</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>A note on health</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-taupe">
        Dear Wander and the writing on this site are for education and general wellbeing. They are not
        medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment, and breathing practices are not a substitute for care
        from a qualified professional. If you're struggling with anxiety, sleep, or compulsive phone use
        in a way that affects your life, please talk to a doctor or a licensed therapist.
      </p>

      <hr class="my-10 border-breath/30" />

      <p>
        Dear Wander is coming to iOS. If any of this feels familiar, you're the person I'm building it for.
        <a href="/app?from=about">Dear Wander is on the App Store</a>, and free to try.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
